  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scoping study land governance in the MENA-region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The scoping study is expected to provide a condensed overview of: 1.	A list of main land governance challenges in the Middle East and Northern Africa (MENA) (possibly per subset of countries), both from a broad land governance perspective, taking into account the different aspects of the Voluntary Guidelines on the Responsible Tenure of Land, Fisheries and Forests (VGGT) and the LAND-at-scale Programme Document; 2.	Regional land governance initiatives (including global initiatives with a regional window), e.g. the Arab Land Conference; 3.	An overview of the donor support and lender support to land governance in the region; and4.	Potential areas for Dutch interventions both in-country and at regional forums in line with the Social Development Goals (SDG&#x2019;s) and the embassy strategies. Special attention is required for cross-cutting themes of gender and climate.</narrative>
  </description>
